:"Which rule should be used first when three side lengths of a non-right triangle are known and one angle is required?","answer_data":{"answer":"Cosine rule"},"explanation":"The cosine rule relates three sides directly to an angle.","difficulty":"extension","question_style":"conceptual","calculator":"neutral","estimated_time_seconds":75,"marks_estimate":2,"tags":["cosine rule","conceptual"],"choices":["Sine rule","Cosine rule","Tangent ratio","Pythagoras only"],"correct_choices":["Cosine rule"]},{"seed_id":"50000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000111","is_core":true,"syllabus_code":"SL 3.3","type":"numeric_answer","prompt":"From a point 20 m from a vertical tower, the angle of elevation to its top is 45°. Find the tower height in metres.","answer_data":{"answer":20,"tolerance":0},"explanation":"tan45°=h/20=1, so h=20.","difficulty":"foundation","question_style":"application","calculator":"not_allowed","estimated_time_seconds":35,"marks_estimate":1,"tags":["angle of elevation","application"],"choices":[],"correct_choices":[20]},{"seed_id":"50000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000112","is_core":true,"syllabus_code":"SL 3.3","type":"multiple_choice","prompt":"A bearing of 135° is measured from which direction and in which sense?","answer_data":{"answer":"From north, clockwise"},"explanation":"Three-figure bearings are measured clockwise from north.","difficulty":"standard","question_style":"procedural","calculator":"not_allowed","estimated_time_seconds":60,"marks_estimate":2,"tags":["bearings","procedural"],"choices":["From north, clockwise","From north, anticlockwise","From east, clockwise","From south, clockwise"],"correct_choices":["From north, clockwise"]},{"seed_id":"50000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000113","is_core":true,"syllabus_code":"SL 3.3","type":"true_false","prompt":"An angle of depression from a horizontal line equals the corresponding angle of elevation because the horizontal lines are parallel.","answer_data":{"answer":true},"explanation":"Alternate interior angles are