ht-handed basis satisfies i×j=k.","difficulty":"foundation","question_style":"recall","calculator":"not_allowed","estimated_time_seconds":35,"marks_estimate":1,"tags":["vector product","recall"],"choices":[],"correct_choices":["k"]},{"seed_id":"50000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000154","is_core":true,"syllabus_code":"AHL 3.16","type":"numeric_answer","prompt":"Find the magnitude of (1,0,0)×(0,3,0).","answer_data":{"answer":3,"tolerance":0},"explanation":"The vectors are perpendicular, so |a×b|=|a||b|=3.","difficulty":"standard","question_style":"procedural","calculator":"not_allowed","estimated_time_seconds":60,"marks_estimate":2,"tags":["vector product","area","procedural"],"choices":[],"correct_choices":[3]},{"seed_id":"50000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000155","is_core":true,"syllabus_code":"AHL 3.16","type":"multi_select","prompt":"Select all true statements about a×b.","answer_data":{"answers":["It is perpendicular to a.","It is perpendicular to b.","Its magnitude is |a||b|sinθ."]},"explanation":"The vector product is anti-commutative: b×a=−a×b.","difficulty":"extension","question_style":"conceptual","calculator":"neutral","estimated_time_seconds":75,"marks_estimate":2,"tags":["vector product","properties","conceptual"],"choices":["It is perpendicular to a.","It is perpendicular to b.","Its magnitude is |a||b|sinθ.","a×b=b×a."],"correct_choices":["It is perpendicular to a.","It is perpendicular to b.","Its magnitude is |a||b|sinθ."]},{"seed_id":"50000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000156","is_core":true,"syllabus_code":"AHL 3.17","type":"multiple_choice","prompt":"Which is a normal vector to the plane 2x−3y+z=7?","answer_data":{"answer":"(2,−3,1)"},"explanation":"The Cartesian coefficients give a normal vector.","difficulty":"foundation","question_style":"recall","calculator":"not_allowed","estimated_time_seconds":35,"marks_estimate":1,"tags":["plane equations","normal vector","recall"],"choices":["(2,−3,1)","(2,3,1)","(7,0,0)","(1,1,1)"],"correct_choices":["(2,−3,1)"]},{"seed_id":"50000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000157","is_core":true,"syllabus_code":"AHL 3.17","type":"numeric_answer","prompt":"Does the point (1,2,3) lie on x+2y−z=2? Enter 1 for yes or 0 for no.","answer_data":{"answer":1,"tolerance":0},"explanation":"1+2(2)−3=2, so the point lies on the plane.","difficulty":"standard","question_style":"procedural","calculator":"not_allowed","estimated_time_seconds":60,"marks_estimate":2,"tags":["planes","point test","procedural"],"choices":[],"correct_choices":[1]},{"seed_id":"50000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000158","is_core":true,"syllabus_code":"AHL 3.17","type":"matching","prompt":"Match each plane form to its characteristic data.","answer_data":{"pairs":[{"left":"r=a+λu+μv","right":"Point and two directions"},{"left":"r·n=d","right":"Normal vector"},{"left":"Ax+By+Cz=D","right":"Cartesian coefficients"}]},"explanation":"Each form exposes different geometric information about the plane.","difficulty":"extension","question_style":"conceptual","calculator":"neutral","estimated_time_seconds":75,"marks_estimate":2,"tags":["plane equations","conceptual"],"choices":[],"correct_choices":[]},{"seed_id":"50000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000159","is_core":true,"syllabus_code":"AHL 3.18","type":"multiple_choice","prompt":"A line has direction d and a plane has normal n. The line is parallel to the plane when which condition holds?","answer_data":{"answer":"d·n=0"},"explanation":"A direction parallel to a plane is perpendicular to its normal.","difficulty":"foundation","question_style":"recall","calculator":"not_allowed","estimated_time_seconds":35,"marks_estimate":1,"tags":["line-plane angle","recall"],"choices":["d·n=0","d×n=0","d=n","|d|=|n|"],"correct_choices":["d·n=0"]},{"seed_id":"50000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000160","is_core":true,"syllabus_code":"AHL 3.18","type":"numeric_answer","prompt":"Find the acute angle in degrees between planes with normals (1,0,0) and (1,1,0).","answer_data":{"answer":45,"tolerance":0.01},"explanation":"The angle between planes is the acute angle between normals: cosθ=1/√2.","difficulty":"standard","question_style":"exam_style","calculator":"allowed","estimated_time_seconds":60,"marks_estimate":2,"tags":["angle between planes","exam_style"],"choices":[],"correct_choices":[45]},{"seed_id":"50000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000161","is_core":true,"syllabus_code":"AHL 3.18","type":"true_false","prompt":"The direction of the line of intersection of two non-parallel planes is parallel to the cross product of their normals.","answer_data":{"answer":true},"explanation":"n₁×n₂ is perpendicular to both normals and therefore lies in both planes.","difficulty":"extension","question_style":"conceptual","calculator":"neutral","estimated_time_seconds":75,"marks_estimate":2,"tags":["plane intersections","conceptual"],"choices":["True","False"],"correct_choices":["True"]},{"seed_id":"50000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000162","is_core":false,"syllabus_code":"AHL 3.18","type":"numeric_answer","prompt":"A line has direction vector (1,2,2) and a plane has normal vector (2,−1,2). Find the acute angle between the line and the plane, in degrees, correct to one decimal place.","answer_data":{"answer":26.4,"tolerance":0.1},"explanation":"The angle α between the direction and normal satisfies cosα=4/9, so α≈63.6°. The line-plane angle is 90°−α≈26.4°.","difficulty":"extension","question_style":"exam_style","calculator":"allowed","estimated_time_seconds":90,"marks_estimate":3,"tags":["vectors","line-plane angle","exam_style"],"choices":[],"correct_choices":[26.4]},{"seed_id":"50000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000163","is_core":true,"syllabus_code":"SL 4.1","type":"multiple_choice","prompt":"A school wants opinions from every year group. Which method best ensures each year is represented?","answer_data":{"answer":"Stratified sampling by year group"},"explanation":"Stratification samples from each relevant subgroup.","difficulty":"foundation","question_style":"recall","calculator":"not_allowed","estimated_time_second