_core":true,"syllabus_code":"SL 4.4","type":"true_false","prompt":"A strong correlation between two variables proves that one causes the other.","answer_data":{"answer":false},"explanation":"Correlation alone does not establish causation; lurking variables may explain the association.","difficulty":"extension","question_style":"misconception","calculator":"neutral","estimated_time_seconds":75,"marks_estimate":2,"tags":["correlation","causation","misconception"],"choices":["True","False"],"correct_choices":["False"]},{"seed_id":"50000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000175","is_core":false,"syllabus_code":"SL 4.4","type":"multi_select","prompt":"For a dataset, Pearson’s correlation coefficient is r=0.82 and the y-on-x regression line is used for prediction. Select all justified statements.","answer_data":{"answers":["There is a strong positive linear association.","A prediction inside the observed x-range is generally safer than a distant extrapolation."]},"explanation":"A large positive r indicates strong positive linear association, not causation. Predict y from x with the y-on-x line and avoid unsupported extrapolation.","difficulty":"extension","question_style":"conceptual","calculator":"neutral","estimated_time_seconds":75,"marks_estimate":3,"tags":["correlation","regression","extrapolation","conceptual"],"choices":["There is a strong positive linear association.","The value of r proves that increasing x causes y to increase.","A prediction inside the observed x-range is generally safer than a distant extrapolation.","The x-on-y regression line should be used to predict y from x."],"correct_choices":["There is a strong positive linear association.","A prediction inside the observed x-range is generally safer than a distant extrapolation."]},{"seed_id":"50000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000176","is_core":true,"syllabus_code":"SL 4.5","type":"numeric_answer","prompt":"A fair die is rolled 60 times. Find the expected number of sixes.","answer_data":{"answer":10,"tolerance":0},